==== Flash Layout ====
===== NOR flash =====

The GL-B2200 has one 16 MiB SPI flash chip.

^ Factory Layout for 16 MiB SPI Flash //(spi0.0: Winbond W25Q128)// ^^^^^^^^^
^ Layer0      | Raw NOR, Partitions from device tree ||||||||
^ Layer1      | mtd0            | mtd1            | mtd2            | mtd3            | mtd4            | mtd5            | mtd6            | mtd7            |
^ Layer2      |                 |                 |                 |                 |                 |                 |                 |                 |
^ Address     | ''0x0000 0000'' | ''0x0004 0000'' | ''0x0006 0000'' | ''0x000c 0000'' | ''0x000d 0000'' | ''0x000e 0000'' | ''0x000f 0000'' | ''0x0017 0000'' |
^ Size        | 256 KiB         | 128 KiB         | 384 KiB         | 64 KiB          | 64 KiB          | 64 KiB          | 512 KiB         | 64 KiB          |
^ Name **\\
  ** | **<abbr>0:SBL1 [Secondary Boot Loader]</abbr>\\
  ** | **<abbr>0:MIBIB [Multi-Image Boot Info Block]</abbr>\\
  ** | **<abbr>0:QSEE [Qualcomm Secure Execution Environment]</abbr>\\
  ** | **<abbr>0:CDT [Configuration Data Table]</abbr>\\
  ** | **<abbr>0:DDRPARAMS [DDR Parameters]</abbr>\\
  ** | **<abbr>0:APPSBLENV [Applications Processor Secondary Boot Loader Environment]</abbr>\\
  ** | **<abbr>0:APPSBL [Applications Processor Secondary Boot Loader]</abbr>\\
  ** | **<abbr>0:ART [Atheros Radio Test]</abbr>\\
  ** |
^ Usage //\\
  // | //Qualcomm\\ Bootloader ELF\\
  // | //Qualcomm\\ Partition Table\\
  // | //Qualcomm\\ TrustZone ELF\\
  // | //Qualcomm\\ Config\\
  // | //¿\\
  // | //U-Boot\\ Environment\\
  // | //U-Boot\\ ELF\\
  // | //Wi-Fi\\ Calibration\\
  // |

