==== Opening the case ====

**Note:** This will void your warranty!

  - Remove the top hat using a plastic prying tool as a lever. There are 5 plastic clips to remove. :!: Be careful, this might leave marks on the plastic case.
  - Remove the rubber feet and unscrew the 3 screws.
  - Gently slide the PCB out of the case. :!: The LEDs are plugged with an extension cable to the case.
  - Unplug the LED cable.
  - Unscrew the 2 screws holding the bottom case.
  - You are now able to access the UART pins.
  - If necessary, you can also remove the 8 screws holding the heat sinks (4 on both faces) in order to access the whole PCB.

